# For each CLUSTER, choose one.
# 
#   campaign  The members are one supplied text. An organisation wrote it and
#             people sent it. Wording may vary -- campaign tools paraphrase --
#             but there is one source document behind them.
# 
#   organic   The members each wrote their own, and the pipeline grouped them
#             because they happen to make a similar point. Ten thousand people
#             independently saying "this rule is too weak" is public opinion,
#             not a mailing list.
# 
#   mixed     A real campaign with genuinely independent submissions swept in
#             alongside it.
# 
#   unusable  Cannot tell from the excerpts shown.
# 
# If torn between `campaign` and `organic`, choose `organic`. Calling genuine
# public opinion a campaign is the error that erases people from the record;
# the reverse merely undercounts coordination.
# 
# Keys: c=campaign  o=organic  m=mixed  u=unusable
{"cluster": 0, "band": "2-3", "size": 2, "label": "", "member_ids": ["FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-2251", "FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-3384"], "members": ["I strongly, strongly oppose ANY changes to the Endangered Species Act (\"ESA\") as proposed by the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service and the National Marine Fisheries Service (NMFS). As a taxpaying citizen, I WANT my tax dollars to go toward strengthening our terrestrial and marine wildlife and their ecosystems. Despite the claim from politicians that only a minority of species have recovered after endangered species listing, the fact is the Endangered Species Act is our nations most effective law for protecting wildlife in danger of extinction, and has prevented 99 percent of listed species from g", "I write to vigorously oppose the proposed rule changes to the Endangered Species Act (ESA) proposed by the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service (FWS) and the National Marine Fisheries Service (NMFS). Despite the claim from politicians that only a minority of species have recovered after endangered species listing, the fact is the ESA is America's most effective law for protecting wildlife in danger of extinction, having prevented 99% of listed species from going extinct. Weakening the ESA by the proposed changes will have dramatic implications for species conservation at a time when the threats to a"]}
{"cluster": 1, "band": "2-3", "size": 3, "label": "", "member_ids": ["FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-0279", "FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-0341", "FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-0436"], "members": ["Protect threatened species. Endangered species are already on emergency life-support, while threatened species are headed for the hospital. But the Trump administration proposes reducing legal protections for threatened species. Dont weaken protections for threatened species. Use only the best available science. The Endangered Species Act does not allow agencies to use economic calculations to influence whether a plant or animal should be protected. Only the best available science can be used. But now the administration wants to allow short-term costs to play a role in how we choose to protect", "Protect threatened species. Endangered species are already on emergency life-support, while threatened species are headed for the hospital. But the Trump administration proposes reducing legal protections for threatened species. Dont weaken protections for threatened species. Use only the best available science. The Endangered Species Act does not allow agencies to use economic calculations to influence whether a plant or animal should be protected. Only the best available science can be used. But now the administration wants to allow short-term costs to play a role in how we choose to protect", "Protect threatened species. Endangered species are already in danger and threatened species are more at risk every day. Do not allow the Trump administration to reduce legal protections for threatened species. Dont weaken protections for threatened species. The Endangered Species Act does not allow agencies to use economic calculations to influence whether a plant or animal should be protected. Only the best available science can be used. But now the administration wants to allow short-term costs to play a role in how we choose to protect the most vulnerable species on the planet. Dont allow e"]}
{"cluster": 2, "band": "2-3", "size": 2, "label": "", "member_ids": ["FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-8682", "FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-8695"], "members": ["I remember how our rivers and air looked and smelled in 1970. I know how close we came to extinction of so many species. I know that we as humans have choices in where we live, how we make our living, how we grow our food. Plants and animals, rivers and estuaries do not. Our actions must not contribute to their degradation. We must act as if we really do understand that the ecosystem acts as our lungs, our liver, our spleen. We must rely on the truth of good, rigorous, peer reviewed science including science that uses confidential human data. PLEASE do not abandon all of the work that so many ", "The Endangered Species Act is one of the most effective conservation laws in the United States. Ninety-nine percent of listed species have been saved from extinction, including iconic species such as the bald eagle. The law is also widely popular; polling shows that 90 percent of voters across the political spectrum support the law. The proposed changes to the statute will weaken the law and put thousands of plant and animal species at risk. The changes proposed to remove the language that ensures listing decisions are made without considering economic impact go against the very nature of the "]}
{"cluster": 3, "band": "2-3", "size": 2, "label": "", "member_ids": ["FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-0759", "FWS-HQ-ES-2018-0006-8541"], "members": ["One of the strongest center pieces of the Endangered Species Act of 1973 has been its reliance on science. Man must understand the world in which he lives so he may act and live accordingly, making sure our world remains habitable for all of the earths living creatures, including us. Since we are called to be good stewards of this planet, we cannot and should not take that responsibility lightly. We need to use the knowledge we gain to make sure we make those decisions appropriately. The minute we start to sacrifice or hold to a different calling, we are sacrificing the world as we know it. Th", "One of the strongest center pieces of the Endangered Species Act of 1973 has been its reliance on science. Man must understand the world in which he lives so he may act and live accordingly, making sure our world remains habitable for all of the earths living creatures, including us. Since we are called to be good stewards of this planet, we cannot and should not take that responsibility lightly. We need to use the knowledge we gain to make sure we make those decisions appropriately. The minute we start to sacrifice or hold to a different calling, we are sacrificing the world as we know it. Th"]}
